      "observed": "R4 pin 2 is connected to GND, tying J8 pin 3 to ground through 1 kΩ. R11 and R12 pin 1 are also connected to GND, so the channel-2 bus pins J1/J2 pin 20 and pin 22 are shorted to GND through 0 Ω jumpers. There is no /PWM2 net in the netlist.",
      "expected": "R4 pin 2 should connect to the PWM2 GPIO net, and R11/R12 pin 1 should connect to that same PWM2 net, as R3/R4 are series resistors from PWM1/PWM2 to J3/J8 pin 3 and R9-R12 select the bus pins supplying PWM1/PWM2.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R4\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R11\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"R12\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R4 Net-_J8-Pin_3_ 0 1k"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "R11 0 /PWM2_C1 0"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "R3, R4 | 1k each | Series resistors from the PWM1/PWM2 GPIO nets to J3 pin 3 / J8 pin 3 respectively."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "PWM channel 2 cannot drive the tilt servo; J8 pin 3 is held low through 1 kΩ. In serial mode, R4 also loads the shared TTL bus to ground, and the selected channel-2 M5Stack GPIO pins are shorted to GND through the 0 Ω jumpers.",
      "confidence": 0.97
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files show a clear miswiring of the second PWM channel: PWM2 is absent and R4/R11/R12 connect the channel-2 signal and bus pins to GND instead of the intended PWM2 net."
}

